# Build steps whose work nothing runs automatically, and why that is correct.
#
# Enforced in both directions by build/step_coverage.zig. The live graph owns
# task identity; tooling/verification_routes.zig owns external executable argv
# shared with the sequential driver. Every dependency closure must be reached
# by aggregate test, a declared per-commit/release route, or a reason here.
# Comments and display labels provide no coverage. Rows for covered or deleted
# tasks fail the same gate.
#
# One row per (step, reason slug). A row is a claim that this step is an
# operation a human asks for, not a check that was wired and forgotten. That
# distinction is the whole point: `scripts/test-examples.sh` was documented as
# outside `zig build test` and run only from verify.sh, so 56 example suites
# went unrun while `zig build test` reported a pass.
#
# The list only ratchets down. Adding a row is a deliberate widening.

# Manual run commands. `zig build run -- handler.ts` and `zig build cli -- ...`
# start a process for a human to interact with; there is no verdict to consume.
run interactive
cli interactive
brief repository-navigation

# Runs the deterministic playbook server and blocks. `zig build test` already
# compiles the executable - deliberately, since nothing installs it and a break
# would otherwise surface only when somebody ran this by hand - so what is
# uncovered here is the server run, not the build.
zttp-standin interactive-server

# Measurements, not assertions. Both print numbers and pass regardless, so
# there is no failure for a gate to catch. The gated forms exist and do run:
# `bench-check` compares against benchmarks/perf-baseline.json in the release
# script, and `test-compile-bench` runs the unit tests behind the compile benchmarks.
bench measurement
compile-bench measurement
production-branch-metric-json measurement

# Replaces the committed performance baseline and refuses dirty source. A
# release maintainer runs it explicitly after deciding to recalibrate.
bench-record release-operation

# Needs a local MLX server, which this project never starts or manages. The
# absence from the aggregate step is stated at its definition in build/host_tests.zig.
test-expert-mlx-e2e needs-local-server

# These commands compute and render publication evidence. The publication
# shells invoke them after clean-source checks. Their native tests run under
# `zig build test`; only the release operations remain manual.
coverage-union release-operation
evidence-publish release-operation

# A mutation run uses a fresh Zig cache for each row. The 231-row run took
# 98.81 seconds on this machine. Run this explicit gate while strengthening
# the acceptance suite.
test-proof-checker-mutants slow-mutation-probe

# Rewrites tests/corpus/**/*.diag from the current check output. The verdict
# lives in `test-diagnostic-corpus`, which `zig build test` runs and which fails
# when a golden and the check disagree. This is the write half: a human runs it
# after changing a case or a diagnostic, reads every golden diff against the
# case's stated intent, and commits it. Wiring it into a check would defeat the
# gate, because a build that rewrites its own expected output never disagrees.
diagnostic-corpus-write regeneration

# The canonical sequential gate is an operator entry point, never recursively
# invoked by its own task coverage. Its constituent routes are checked.
verify sequential-verification-driver

# Shadow evaluator evidence deliberately stays outside production/aggregate
# verdicts until P9 meets every frozen precision and semantic expectation.
flow-shadow-diff shadow-differential-evidence
